gal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}{U}","name":"Twincast","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","oracle_text":"Copy target instant or sorcery spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2009-07-17","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If Moonlace is cast on a spell that becomes a permanent (a creature spell, an artifact spell, or an enchantment spell), the permanent will enter colorless and will remain colorless until it leaves the battlefield (or until another effect changes its color).","oracle_id":"52d4dc8a-2799-4b4e-9c20-f14bb75c2279","published_at":"2006-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Moonlace's effect doesn't wear off.","oracle_id":"52d4dc8a-2799-4b4e-9c20-f14bb75c2279","published_at":"2006-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell has damage divided as it was cast, the division can't be changed, although the targets receiving that damage still can. The same is true of spells that distribute counters.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell that's copied has an X whose value was determined as it was cast, the copy will have the same value of X.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell that's copied is modal (that is, it says \"Choose one —\" or the like), the copy will have the same mode. A different mode can't be chosen.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copy is created on the stack, so it's not \"cast.\" Abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell won't trigger. The copy will resolve before the original spell does.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copy will have the same targets as the spell it's copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. If, for one of the targets, you can't choose a new legal target, then it remains unchanged (even if the current target is illegal).","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Twincast can copy any instant or sorcery spell, not just one with targets.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can't choose to pay any alternative or additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any alternative or additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy.","oracle_id":"8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision to counter a spell or destroy a permanent is a decision made on announcement before the target is selected. If the spell is redirected, this mode can't be changed, so only targets of the selected type are valid.","oracle_id":"b94c0336-2ca8-4bb1-bb1f-e9babd1826ad","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Hydroblast can target any spell or permanent, not just a red one. It checks the color of the target only on resolution.","oracle_id":"b94c0336-2ca8-4bb1-bb1f-e9babd1826ad","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won’t return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an Aura is put onto the battlefield without being cast, the Aura’s controller-to-be chooses what it will enchant as it comes back onto the battlefield. An Aura put onto the battlefield this way doesn’t target anything (so it could be attached to an opponent’s permanent with hexproof, for example), but the Aura’s enchant ability restricts what it can be attached to. If the Aura can’t legally be attached to anything, it remains in its current zone.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it’s considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners’ graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision to counter a spell or destroy a permanent is a decision made on announcement before the target is selected. If the spell is redirected, this mode can't be changed, so only targets of the selected type are valid.","oracle_id":"ecc435e2-deb1-420a-a79f-01dd08747314","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Pyroblast can target any spell or permanent, not just a blue one. It checks the color of the target only on resolution.","oracle_id":"ecc435e2-deb1-420a-a79f-01dd08747314","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
